>> title: Hong Kong French Toast
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: bread, eggs, peanut butter, deep-fried, hong kong
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: french toast, hong kong french toast, 西多士, sai do si, sai dor si, HK french toast, western toast, kowloon french toast, deep fried french toast, peanut butter french toast, 西多
>> pairs-with: french-toast, hong-kong-milk-tea
>> servings: 2
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: narrow — oil under 350°F soaks into the crumb instead of sealing it, and a soggy 西多士 will not crisp back up

Not the diner's french toast — the peanut butter goes inside and it is deep-fried rather than griddled.

>> step: spread the peanut butter inside, press to two
Spread @creamy peanut butter{3%Tbs}(50 g) over @white sandwich bread{4%slices}(thick-cut, crusts off) and press them into two sandwiches.

>> step: beat the egg loose
Beat @eggs{2%large} with @evaporated milk{2%Tbs}(30 mL) in a wide shallow #dish{}.

>> step: coat every face, edges too
Turn @&(~2)sandwiches{} through @&(~1)beaten egg{} on every face, edges included, until they are wet right through.

>> step: deep-fry 350°F, 90 sec, turn once
Fry @&(~1)coated sandwiches{} in @neutral oil{3%cups}(700 mL; 1 in deep, held at 350°F) ~fry{90%sec}, turning once, until they are deep gold, then stand them on a rack.

>> step: lay the cold butter on top, syrup over
Lay @salted butter{2%Tbs}(cold, in a 1/4-in slab) on @&(~1)hot toast{} and pour @golden syrup{2%Tbs}(30 mL) over it at the table.
